<!--
  PARTIAL/INCLUDE: this file is never rendered on its own - home.ejs and
  about.ejs each include this header partial near the top and the sibling
  footer.ejs partial near the bottom, so together the three files form ONE
  complete HTML document per page. That's why the closing body/html tags
  live in footer.ejs instead of here - closing them in this file would end
  the document before each page's own content (the heading, the product
  list, etc.) ever got a chance to render, leaving that content floating
  outside the html element as invalid HTML.
  NOTE: deliberately not writing the actual include-tag syntax in this
  comment - EJS scans the whole file for its delimiters regardless of HTML
  comment boundaries, so literal example tags here would be executed for
  real instead of staying inert documentation (this bit us once already).
-->
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Document</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <h1>EJS Template Header</h1>
    </header>
